00:29:10.715 --> 00:29:13.685
And then the liberals just
want everything goes, right,

00:29:13.685 --> 00:29:15.620 align:start size:88% position:13%
kind of this
libertinism or whatever.

00:29:15.620 --> 00:29:18.656
But that's really not the
fight we're in anymore.

00:29:18.656 --> 00:29:22.360 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, Sam Smith, by
putting those devil horns on,

00:29:22.360 --> 00:29:25.463 align:start size:81% position:19%
is actually making
a moral claim.

00:29:25.463 --> 00:29:26.865
And it's what you're saying,

00:29:26.865 --> 00:29:29.033 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's that the transgression
is somehow valuable,

00:29:29.033 --> 00:29:31.402
that like, this is what
you should strive for.

00:29:31.402 --> 00:29:34.706 align:start position:0%
And the ugliness therefore
also becomes part of the point,

00:29:34.706 --> 00:29:36.541
like it's in service
of that performance

00:29:36.541 --> 00:29:39.878
that there's really nothing
of value or virtue in it.

00:29:39.878 --> 00:29:41.946
Otherwise, it kind of
sucks that the song

00:29:41.946 --> 00:29:43.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
is like kind of
overplayed and also over-

00:29:43.548 --> 00:29:46.184 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Right. Well it was just
like, give me something here,

00:29:46.184 --> 00:29:48.987
give me something here
so that it is not just

00:29:48.987 --> 00:29:50.455
what it obviously is.

00:29:50.455 --> 00:29:52.423 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I don't sense that there
was anything else there,

00:29:52.423 --> 00:29:53.958
but right, so we're
already sort of into

00:29:53.958 --> 00:29:58.797
the crisis of religion here.
So does Sam Smith need God?

00:30:00.198 --> 00:30:02.667 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I think Sam Smith has a
God, I think he's picked one.

00:30:02.667 --> 00:30:05.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, genuinely, I think
like this is kind of,

00:30:05.837 --> 00:30:08.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
we've been talking around
this a little bit now

00:30:08.039 --> 00:30:11.309
that like there really is
no such thing as atheism.

00:30:12.777 --> 00:30:15.580
This is something that the
Bible has this great line,

00:30:15.580 --> 00:30:18.583
"The fool hath set in his
heart there is no God."

00:30:18.583 --> 00:30:20.652
And people kind of
read that and think

00:30:20.652 --> 00:30:22.420
that that means like the fool,

00:30:22.420 --> 00:30:24.055
it's foolish to be an atheist.

00:30:24.055 --> 00:30:26.858 align:start size:81% position:19%
It's stupid to
believe in no God.

00:30:26.858 --> 00:30:28.293 align:start size:84% position:16%
But there's a
deeper level to it,

00:30:28.293 --> 00:30:31.296 align:start size:88% position:13%
which is that only a
fool can deceive himself

00:30:31.296 --> 00:30:32.997 align:start size:84% position:16%
into believing
that nothing serves

00:30:32.997 --> 00:30:34.732
the role of God in his life.

00:30:34.732 --> 00:30:36.901 align:start size:84% position:16%
That there's nothing
in that place

00:30:36.901 --> 00:30:39.537
of highest good, highest power.

00:30:39.537 --> 00:30:41.105
And so I think, you know,

00:30:41.105 --> 00:30:43.441
this is what you
see when you see

00:30:43.441 --> 00:30:44.909
the kneelers at BLM rallies,

00:30:44.909 --> 00:30:46.911
when you see Sam
Smith, you know,

00:30:46.911 --> 00:30:49.747 align:start size:84% position:16%
like offering a
sacrifice on the altar

00:30:49.747 --> 00:30:52.717 align:start size:84% position:16%
of kind of like
ugliness and illogic.

00:30:52.717 --> 00:30:55.286
These are people
who just worship

00:30:55.286 --> 00:30:57.989
just as profoundly or as
intensely as you or I,

00:30:57.989 --> 00:30:59.791
they just don't know
that they're doing it.

00:30:59.791 --> 00:31:01.492
And that's kind
of where, I mean,

00:31:01.492 --> 00:31:04.128
the Bible has lots of
passages about this,

00:31:04.128 --> 00:31:06.297 align:start size:97% position:3%
that, you know, when people
start to worship idols,

00:31:06.297 --> 00:31:08.099
they start to forget that
that's what they're doing.

00:31:08.099 --> 00:31:09.868
It's a kind of self deceit.

00:31:09.868 --> 00:31:12.804
And I think all of this
is just like, you know,

00:31:12.804 --> 00:31:15.173 align:start size:88% position:13%
it's kind of unnecessary
because it's based

00:31:15.173 --> 00:31:18.343
on this false assumption
that in order to be smart,

00:31:18.343 --> 00:31:20.511
in order to be rational,
in order to be scientific,

00:31:20.511 --> 00:31:23.681
we can't possibly say that
the thing we're worshiping

00:31:23.681 --> 00:31:27.552 align:start size:97% position:3%
is actual God, like, as
actual an object of worship.

00:31:27.552 --> 00:31:29.387 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's kind of the
crisis of religion,

00:31:29.387 --> 00:31:31.189
which I talk about.
- So if we're going

00:31:31.189 --> 00:31:33.892
on this theme here that
the West is worth saving

00:31:33.892 --> 00:31:35.960
and we're trying
to save the West,

00:31:35.960 --> 00:31:38.496
I assume you don't want
to force all the people

00:31:38.496 --> 00:31:41.099
to be believers or
force all the people

00:31:41.099 --> 00:31:43.768
to have the same religious
beliefs that you might have.

00:31:43.768 --> 00:31:46.037
So how do you blend
those two things?

00:31:46.037 --> 00:31:49.774 align:start size:97% position:3%
A sort of what you describe
as a necessary belief

00:31:49.774 --> 00:31:52.410 align:start size:97% position:3%
for this stuff to be
saved, but also the ability

00:31:52.410 --> 00:31:56.080
to have people and
ideas on the margins.

00:31:56.080 --> 00:31:57.315
- Right. I mean,

00:31:57.315 --> 00:32:00.718 align:start size:88% position:13%
I think that forcing
somebody into a religion

00:32:00.718 --> 00:32:02.387 align:start size:84% position:16%
is kind of a
contradiction in terms

00:32:02.387 --> 00:32:04.055
and that's part of the illogic

00:32:04.055 --> 00:32:06.457 align:start size:84% position:16%
that made this stuff
so distasteful.

00:32:06.457 --> 00:32:09.027 align:start position:0%
When you force somebody to
convert at the point of a sword,

00:32:09.027 --> 00:32:11.429 align:start size:88% position:13%
you basically have
created a false belief.

00:32:11.429 --> 00:32:12.664
It's just somebody
saying something

00:32:12.664 --> 00:32:14.399
to get out of getting
killed essentially.

00:32:14.399 --> 00:32:17.402
And so not only is
that inherently bad,

00:32:17.402 --> 00:32:18.970 align:start size:81% position:19%
but it doesn't
solve the problem,

00:32:18.970 --> 00:32:21.005
which is that what you're
really dealing with is

00:32:21.005 --> 00:32:24.008
a void in people's hearts.

00:32:24.008 --> 00:32:25.910
And so what I say in
the book is like, look,

00:32:25.910 --> 00:32:28.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would love it if
everybody tomorrow became

00:32:28.880 --> 00:32:31.916
the specific kind of
Christian that I am

00:32:31.916 --> 00:32:34.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
and went to my church
and said the Nicene Creed

00:32:34.619 --> 00:32:37.822
every week and whatever, I
think that would be good.

00:32:37.822 --> 00:32:41.559
But I'm not here to like
write a law that says that,

00:32:41.559 --> 00:32:44.195
I'm not here even to like
bang you over the head

00:32:44.195 --> 00:32:45.697
with my Bible.

00:32:45.697 --> 00:32:49.500 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm just here to say that
actually, you already believe

00:32:49.500 --> 00:32:52.770 align:start size:88% position:13%
certain things that
imply this higher power,

00:32:52.770 --> 00:32:54.539
and we should 'fess up to that.

00:32:54.539 --> 00:32:56.708
Like, just by getting out
of bed in the morning,

00:32:56.708 --> 00:32:59.978 align:start position:0%
you sort of concede that there's
some reason to do things.

00:32:59.978 --> 00:33:02.080
And once you say there's
a reason to do things,

00:33:02.080 --> 00:33:04.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
then you have to say
there is a highest reason

00:33:04.582 --> 00:33:07.552
some good toward which
all those goods aim.

00:33:07.552 --> 00:33:09.721
And I say in the book,
it's less a conversion

00:33:09.721 --> 00:33:12.790
than a surrender. We
ought to, you know,

00:33:12.790 --> 00:33:15.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
not be ashamed of being
honest about the fact that

00:33:15.860 --> 00:33:18.062 align:start size:84% position:16%
mankind has a
spiritual dimension

00:33:18.062 --> 00:33:20.932
and we can look directly
at that without feeling

00:33:20.932 --> 00:33:23.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
like we're, you know,
primitive or superstitious

00:33:23.501 --> 00:33:24.936
or what have you.

00:33:24.936 --> 00:33:27.405 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's actually the other thing
that makes us primitive,

00:33:27.405 --> 00:33:29.774 align:start size:84% position:16%
denying that there's
a spiritual realm

00:33:29.774 --> 00:33:32.777
is what turns us into kind of
primitive worshipers of Fauci

00:33:32.777 --> 00:33:35.179
or BLM or whatever.

00:33:35.179 --> 00:33:38.483
- You've given me a fine
segue to the fifth here,

00:33:38.483 --> 00:33:41.152
which is crisis of regime
because we seem to have

00:33:41.152 --> 00:33:44.155 align:start size:84% position:16%
a bunch of people
that worship a regime

00:33:44.155 --> 00:33:48.726
that has very little to do
with their interests in mind.

00:33:48.726 --> 00:33:51.396
That kind of sums up to me
where we're at politically

00:33:51.396 --> 00:33:52.830
at the moment.

00:33:52.830 --> 00:33:54.766 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I don't mean just us
from an American perspective,

00:33:54.766 --> 00:33:56.801
I think kind of all over
the world at the moment.

00:33:56.801 --> 00:33:58.169
- That's right, that's right.

00:33:58.169 --> 00:34:01.305 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, I talk in this
section of the book

00:34:01.305 --> 00:34:03.074
about the classical
theory of regimes

00:34:03.074 --> 00:34:05.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
and about what a republic
is supposed to be

00:34:05.943 --> 00:34:09.013 align:start size:97% position:3%
because that's what we're
supposed to be is a republic.

00:34:09.013 --> 00:34:11.449
And part of the point
of a republic is that

00:34:11.449 --> 00:34:15.787
"You rule and are ruled in
turn," as Aristotle says,

00:34:15.787 --> 00:34:19.991
nobody is born, you know,
with spurs on his boots

00:34:19.991 --> 00:34:22.627
and nobody is born
to be subjugated.

00:34:22.627 --> 00:34:25.530 align:start size:88% position:13%
We have a kind of shared
distribution of power

00:34:25.530 --> 00:34:29.867 align:start size:97% position:3%
that doesn't flatten
everybody out into sameness,

00:34:29.867 --> 00:34:32.103
but does give people,
you know, ownership.

00:34:32.103 --> 00:34:35.406 align:start size:84% position:16%
Each person has
ownership sovereignty
over his own choices.

00:34:35.406 --> 00:34:36.674 align:start size:84% position:16%
And yeah, you're
seeing a lot of people

00:34:36.674 --> 00:34:40.011
that like don't want
that or are falling for

00:34:40.011 --> 00:34:42.914
the kind of removal of that.

00:34:42.914 --> 00:34:45.149 align:start size:84% position:16%
And what I identify
in the book is kind of

00:34:45.149 --> 00:34:49.153 align:start size:97% position:3%
the problem here is the
breakdown of what the ancients

00:34:49.153 --> 00:34:50.354
would've called filia.

00:34:50.354 --> 00:34:52.657 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's friendship,
just civic friendship,

00:34:52.657 --> 00:34:56.294 align:start size:84% position:16%
just the love between
fellow citizens.

00:34:56.294 --> 00:34:59.430 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, we haven't heard
the state of the union address

00:34:59.430 --> 00:35:02.300 align:start size:88% position:13%
yet, but I'll be willing
to bet that Biden,

00:35:02.300 --> 00:35:05.903
